an exact line fits its rate and intercept: true
points without operations are not fitted: true
a time that does not grow with the operations fits nothing: true
one operation count fits nothing: true
on CUDA/HIP every swept extent is timed, seeded as one scalar kernel's contraction: true
on CUDA/HIP the kernel's operations grow with the reduction extent: true
where the seeded default does not apply, the sweep refuses rather than time the default: true
the fill fit recovers the saturating threads and the full-fill rate: true
the pre-fill fit over a partially filled launch reads the full-fill rate times its fill: true
under the fill model the same sweep reads the full-fill rate: true
the uncapped form fits the capped sweep worse: true
a sweep that never leaves full fill identifies no saturation: true
a point with tile-MMA work refuses: the fill is a scalar fit: true
a single geometry whose every point is partial identifies no saturation: true
the rate is the caller's lead geometry's, whatever the series' names sort to: true
fewer than three points refuse: true
on a GPU backend every launch point is timed, one scalar context of 64-thread blocks: true
on a GPU backend the launch's blocks grow with the output: true
without the GPU sketch family the launch sweep refuses: true
